  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is our best result at 0.591 acc, substantially outperforming config_001 (singleprofile, 0.485), confirming multiprofile aggregation adds significant value. However, we have not yet tested whether the aggregation mechanism itself (avgpool vs transformer) matters. Question: config_003 isolates a single variable—aggregation (transformer vs avgpool)—holding RNA encoder (pca_n2000), profile setting (multiprofile), and modality (rna_only) constant. This directly tests whether a learned, attention-based aggregation of multiple profiles captures inter-profile interactions that simple averaging misses. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It is the cleanest single-variable comparison to our strongest result, reducing confounding; (2) the aggregation choice is a foundational design decision that will propagate to all future multimodal experiments, so resolving it early saves budget; (3) if transformer aggregation yields a meaningful gain over avgpool, it justifies investing in transformer-based configs for subsequent encoder and fusion tests; if not, we confirm avgpool suffices and can redirect budget toward encoder or fusion questions. This balances exploitation (building on the best config) with targeted exploration of an important, untested design axis."
}

